Found 2026-08-28 while building k79 step 6 for containers.

Measured:

  perl -Ilib -MAPI::Docker::Type::ContainerSummary \
    -e 'print API::Docker::Type::ContainerSummary->can("croak") ? "leaks" : "no"'
  -> leaks

API::Docker::Role::Type does `use Moo::Role; use Carp qw( croak ); use
Scalar::Util qw( blessed );` and never `use namespace::clean;`. Everything
imported after `use Moo::Role` is composed into the consumer as a method, so
every generated class answers ->croak and ->blessed. Not harmful today; it is
two names in a namespace that is otherwise exactly the daemon's fields plus a
documented handful, and the next collision is silent.

The other two roles in this distribution get it right:
API::Docker::Role::Filters and API::Docker::Role::Using both close with
`use namespace::clean;` on the line after their imports.

The fix is that one line. It changes the method surface of 201 classes
(removing two accidental entries), so it wants its own commit and a run of
prove -lr t/ rather than being folded into something else.

Done in 3dfc6ae, alone as the ticket asked. Verified independently after: ->croak and ->blessed are gone from a generated class, while BUILDARGS still files an unknown key into unknown_fields and the from_data croak still fires -- namespace::clean took nothing the role needs. The agent measured each internal site rather than trusting the mechanism, including the collision croak in _entity_attribute_index that no test covers, and mutation-checked its own assertion by removing the line again. Nothing in the repo called either method, so a green run alone would not have settled it -- which is why the ticket was right to ask.
